# inbox's reply golden set (core/modules/inbox/README.md "The reply golden set"): an Owner's or an
# Admin's session, inbox.export; the route is Owner only since gamma-p7-060 (exports are, F18 §4), and
# a Member's session is refused 403 forbidden. The answer is a file, not JSON: a JSON line per labeled
# reply with its channel, the owner's class, the classification and the conversation before it, the
# person's names masked and no id, also written under the workspace's exports/. The file is the
# caller's own (gamma-p6-060): the labeled replies of your own threads only; the operator's
# `pnpm inbox:export-labels` holds every member's.

### GET /v1/workspaces/{workspaceId}/inbox/exports/reply-labels.jsonl: every labeled reply of your own threads, its latest label, with the thread's messages before it (the latest ten), also written to exports/reply-labels-<UTC date>.jsonl; 413 files_too_large past 25 MiB
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/workspaces/{{workspaceId}}/inbox/exports/reply-labels.jsonl
Accept: application/jsonl
Cookie: {{sessionCookie}}

### GET /v1/workspaces/{workspaceId}/inbox/exports/reply-labels.jsonl?week: the labels chosen in one ISO week (UTC), written to exports/reply-labels-<ISO week>.jsonl, the day's full file left in place; 400 week_invalid for a week its year does not have or one not started
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/workspaces/{{workspaceId}}/inbox/exports/reply-labels.jsonl?week=2026-W44
Accept: application/jsonl
Cookie: {{sessionCookie}}
